|Name Origin=Noxdeus fuses "nox" (Latin for night) and "deus" (Latin for god), symbolizing a divine being born from eternal darkness.
|Main Details=Noxdeus is said to manifest only during lunar eclipses, when the veil between worlds thins. Its arrival silences the wild and chills the air. It feeds on fear, growing stronger with each heartbeat steeped in dread.

Known only as "The God of the Night", no records explain its origin. Some believe it was once a celestial guardian, corrupted by cosmic imbalance.

Long ago, a forgotten civilization worshipped Noxdeus to ward off nightmares and protect their dreams. They built obsidian temples and offered memories to appease it. When the stars aligned in a rare celestial event, Noxdeus vanished—until now. Trainers who encounter it report strange dreams and a lingering chill that never fades.
